{"toolCallId":"call_0a91505edf8943ed83b96f1e7541a08b","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"13:// work. Repairing only the first kind is the whole point: a tool that filled in\n16:// Dry by default; --apply writes. Everything --apply will write is named by the\n118:const USAGE = 'Usage: repair-derived.cjs [--folder <packet>]... [--roots <dir>] [--apply]';\n146:// stderr is the only account of why the packet could not be read.\n198:// only one silently reports half the fleet as having nothing wrong.\n367:  // alone. Filling only an absent field made drift permanent: the scaffold\n469:      what: `packet pointer -> ${pointer}`,\n474:          throw new Error('the packet pointer left the frontmatter between the report and the write');\n600:function parseArgs(argv) {\n601:  // --folder repeats. A caller with a known set of packets would otherwise pay\n606:  for (let i = 0; i < argv.length; i += 1) {\n607:    const token = argv[i];\n608:    if (token === '--apply') {\n610:    } else if (token === '--folder' || token === '--roots') {\n611:      const value = argv[i + 1];\n613:      if (token === '--folder') options.folders.push(value);\n620:      // turn a dropped flag name — `repair-derived.cjs specs/one --apply` —\n622:      fail(`unexpected argument: ${token} (paths need --folder or --roots)`);\n638:// the tree and writes outside it. Real paths only ever narrow what is accepted;\n670:  const { apply, folders: folderArgs, roots: rootsArg } = parseArgs(process.argv.slice(2));\n707:        // leave an --apply run without the account of what it already wrote.\n749:    process.stdout.write('\\nNot repairable here — these record work someone did, and only they can write them:\\n');\n768:      ? folderArgs.map((f) => `--folder ${f}`).join(' ')\n770:    process.stdout.write(`\\nTo apply these repairs:\\n  node ${path.relative(REPO, __filename)} ${scope} --apply\\n`);\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-