{"toolCallId":"call_158c542bc6024cb2b1e87fe868e58610","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md:92:| REQ-011 | With `--quiet`, any warning the script writes to stderr is still written to stderr. `--quiet` trims stdout only. |\nspecs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md:50:- [ ] T017 Keep the quiet branch stdout-only: no `2>&1` and no stderr redirection, so every warning still reaches stderr (REQ-011) (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`)\nspecs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/acceptance-criteria.md:65:| AC-012 | REQ-011 | Given a run whose stderr carries a warning, When the same run adds `--quiet`, Then stderr keeps that warning byte for byte and only stdout is trimmed | `diff <(bash recommend-level.sh --loc 50 --files 2 2>&1 >/dev/null) <(bash recommend-level.sh --loc 50 --files 2 --quiet 2>&1 >/dev/null)` reports no difference | Unmet | - |\n=== description.json ===\n{\n  \"specFolder\": \"zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\",\n  \"description\": \"Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\",\n  \"keywords\": [\n    \"quiet\",\n    \"flag\",\n    \"recommend-level\"\n  ],\n  \"lastUpdated\": \"2026-10-26T14:08:42.883Z\",\n  \"specId\": \"001\",\n  \"folderSlug\": \"recommend-level-quiet-flag\",\n  \"parentChain\": [\n    \"zz-bench-authoring\"\n  ],\n  \"memorySequence\": 0,\n  \"memoryNameHistory\": [],\n  \"level\": \"3\"\n}"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w904a7ae601/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"85162b","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
